    "declared": false,
    "version": 1,
    "kind": "certification",
    "proves": "Verify that a crashed service is automatically restarted by systemd and\nre-registers in etcd within 60 seconds.\n\nTest sequence:\n  1. Confirm DNS service is active on node-3 (baseline)\n  2. Kill the DNS systemd unit (simulates process crash / OOM kill)\n  3. Wait up to 60s for systemd to restart it (Restart=on-failure in unit file)\n  4. Assert: DNS unit is active again\n  5. Assert: DNS service is still registered in etcd\n\nDNS is chosen because:\n  - It runs on node-3 (not a control-plane node) \u2014 safe to interrupt\n  - It has no quorum requirements \u2014 a brief outage won't cascade\n  - Its re-registration in etcd proves the full restart path works end-to-end\n\nThis test proves the Restart=on-failure systemd policy is correctly configured\nand that the service reconnects to etcd after restart without operator intervention.",
